---
import Guide from '../../layouts/Guide.astro';
import { url, absoluteUrl } from '../../lib/url';
import { CHECKED, SOURCES } from '../../data/au/facts';
import { GUIDES, PRACTICE } from '../../data/au/guides';
import stats from '../../data/au/app-stats.json';
---
<Guide
  title="About Pledge: Who Makes It and How Facts Are Checked"
  description="An independent study app by an independent developer and student. How facts are checked and dated. Not affiliated with the Australian Government."
  path="about/"
  h1="About Pledge"
  answer="Pledge is an independent iPhone app for the Australian citizenship test, made by Raghav Kant, an independent developer and student. It is not affiliated with or endorsed by the Australian Government. Every fact on this site about the real test is quoted from Home Affairs, with the date it was checked."
  sources={['test', 'prepare', 'booklet']}
  related={[GUIDES.checking, PRACTICE, GUIDES.faq]}
  schema={[{
    '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'Person', '@id': absoluteUrl('about/') + '#author',
    name: 'Raghav Kant', url: absoluteUrl('about/') + '#author', email: 'mailto:pledge.citizenship.help@gmail.com',
    description: 'Independent developer and student. Not a migration agent, lawyer or government official.',
    sameAs: ['https://github.com/raghavkant'],
  }]}
>
  <h2 id="who">Who makes Pledge</h2>
  <p>Pledge is made by Raghav Kant, an independent developer and student. The app has no advertising. You can write to <a href="mailto:pledge.citizenship.help@gmail.com">pledge.citizenship.help@gmail.com</a>.</p>

  <h2 id="author">About the author</h2>
  <p>Raghav Kant is an independent developer and student who writes the guides on this website from the booklet <em>Our Common Bond</em> and Home Affairs sources, and builds the Pledge app. Raghav is not a migration agent, a lawyer or a government official. Every guide carries Raghav’s name, the date its facts were last checked against Home Affairs, and its sources.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>The rules about the test are quoted word for word from Home Affairs; the practice questions are written from <em>Our Common Bond</em>, each with its booklet page.</li>
    <li>The process is set out in <a href={url('about/how-we-check-facts/')}>how we check facts</a>, and every fact is listed with its source and check date in a <a href="https://github.com/raghavkant/pledge/blob/main/docs/facts.md">public facts register</a>.</li>
    <li>Found a mistake? Write to <a href="mailto:pledge.citizenship.help@gmail.com">pledge.citizenship.help@gmail.com</a>.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>This website gives general information, not migration advice.</p>

  <h2 id="not-government">Not a government service</h2>
  <p>Pledge is an independent study app. It is not affiliated with or endorsed by the Australian Government. Home Affairs says: “The Department does not endorse or recommend any external courses that claim to help you prepare for the citizenship test, including paid external apps.” Its own free resources, including the booklet and the practice test, are listed in our <a href={url('australia/') + '#free-resources'}>guide to the test</a>.</p>

  <h2 id="how-facts-are-checked">How facts are checked</h2>
  <p>In short (the full policy is on <a href={url('about/how-we-check-facts/')}>how we check facts</a>):</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Every rule about the real test (the number of questions, the pass mark, the time, the values rule, booking, fees and so on) is quoted from a Home Affairs page, and the page is linked.</li>
    <li>Each guide shows the date the facts were last checked against Home Affairs. The latest check was <time datetime={CHECKED.iso}>{CHECKED.label}</time>.</li>
    <li>Facts are re-checked at least every 90 days, and fees every 1 July.</li>
    <li>If something can’t be confirmed on a Home Affairs page, it isn’t stated. For example, we don’t quote pass rates.</li>
    <li>The booklet guides summarise <a href={SOURCES.booklet}><em>Australian Citizenship: Our Common Bond</em></a> (© Commonwealth of Australia, CC BY 4.0) with its page numbers.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>This site gives general information, not migration advice. For your own situation, contact Home Affairs or a registered migration agent.</p>

  <h2 id="questions">About the practice questions</h2>
  <p>Pledge’s questions are written from the booklet. They are not questions from the real test. This website has Pledge’s free questions only: the {stats.free.part1Questions} Part 1 questions and {stats.free.valuesQuestions} values questions that are also free in the app.</p>

  <h2 id="privacy">Privacy</h2>
  <p>This website uses no cookies, analytics or tracking, and the practice test stores nothing on your device. The app has no account, no ads and no tracking. See the <a href={url('privacy/')}>Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
</Guide>
